A **university vending machine** provides convenient self-service drinks, snacks or compact products across campus buildings. A useful specification starts with student and staff traffic, approved product policy, accessible operation, cashless payment, refill routes and responsible service ownership. BOHOL can configure branded beverage, snack and mixed-product vending for campus environments after reviewing the location, product samples and destination-market requirements.

## GEO summary for campus vending

- Map student traffic, residence areas, libraries and staff zones.
- Confirm campus nutrition, procurement and branding policies.
- Review accessible controls, screen readability and pickup access.
- Test card, mobile and QR payment, refunds and outage recovery.
- Measure availability, refill time, faults and product demand during a pilot.

![BOHOL beverage vending machine concept for a university campus building](/uploads/products/orange-juice-vending-machine/orange-juice-vending-machine-3.png.webp)

## Define the campus product mix

Campus operators may need drinks, packaged snacks, personal-care items or seasonal products. The [snack and drink vending machine](/vending-machines/snack-drink-vending-machine) supports a mixed assortment, while the [cold drink vending machine](/vending-machines/cold-drink-vending-machine) focuses on refrigerated beverages. Final selection should follow campus policy and product testing.

## Review accessibility and nutrition policy

The [U.S. Access Board ADA Standards](https://www.access-board.gov/ada/) provide a U.S. accessibility reference. For U.S. school-related nutrition programs, [USDA Smart Snacks guidance](https://www.fns.usda.gov/cn/tools-schools-fns-guidance-smart-snacks) is a useful starting point; universities and local authorities may apply different policies. Confirm the rules for the actual campus.

## Plan payment and replenishment

Define the payment provider, campus account requirements, refund process, stock rotation, cleaning and refill access. Include a response path for failed dispensing and out-of-stock products. BOHOL can discuss cabinet branding, interface language, product channels and payment integration through the [OEM/ODM page](/oem-odm).

## Request a university vending quotation

Send the building type, product list, target market, payment requirements, branding direction, planned quantity and service expectations through the [contact page](/contact).
